{
  "summary": "Adds edge-case script and transaction test vectors to script_tests.json and tx_invalid.json. The new vectors cover interpreter corners including OP_CHECKSEQUENCEVERIFY with -2, OP_IFDUP on negative zero, OP_ROLL with duplicate values, taproot output keys that are not valid x-coordinates, and single-flag STRICTENC, LOW_S, and NULLFAIL cases.",
  "problem": "Downstream and alternate implementations (such as bitcoin-s) that rely on Bitcoin Core's static test vectors can miss subtle script interpreter edge cases. Additionally, some policy validation cases were previously only caught when Bitcoin Core's C++ test harness injected flags dynamically, leaving consumers of the static JSON vectors without coverage.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author note in PR description: \"These were discovered by finding gaps in an alternate implementation (bitcoin-s)\"",
    "Author note in PR description: \"Some policy cases were only caught by the tx_valid harness adding flags back, which implementations copying the JSON don't replicate.\""
